    "narrative": "The Austin Waves look to capitalize on today\u2019s slate with **Heliot Ramos** and **Jackson Merrill** serving as the core of our offense, both grading out in the \"Strong\" category due to favorable park factors and middle-of-the-order protections. **Andy Pages** also projects well, benefiting from a high-run-environment matchup against an opposing starter with an xERA north of 4.80. Given the premium we place on speed in this 5x5 format, **Nasim Nunez** and **Cole Carrigg** remain on the active roster despite lower raw power projections; their ability to manufacture stolen bases provides a necessary floor for our category density, even if their offensive ceilings are capped by the lower ends of the order.\n\nOur most complex decision centered on **Jorge Polanco**, who slots into the lineup with a 51.30 efficiency score. While he remains a marginal start, his projection is dragged down by a tough matchup against Nola and a 31% rain risk, which threatens to truncate his plate appearances. We considered elevating **Brayan Rocchio** over him to chase better defensive and baserunning upside, but the volatility in **Brayan Rocchio**'s contact profile ultimately kept him on the bench. Meanwhile, our heavy hitters **Kyle Tucker**, **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.**, and **Gunnar Henderson** are all idle due to scheduled off-days, and **Luis Robert Jr.** remains sidelined on the IL, placing an increased burden on **Jordan Westburg**, **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.**, and **Jacob Wilson** to anchor our middle infield production. We are closely monitoring weather reports at the stadium, as any significant delay could necessitate a late-scratch pivot to **Coby Mayo** or **Miguel Vargas** if their respective lineups are finalized in time.",
